    Bug 2022247 - Drop the EWS operation sender's reference on its server upon shutdown. r=edicharry


    I ended up needing to pull in `async-lock` for its `Mutex`, to avoid the rare
    panic if we end up shutting down at the same time we're e.g. computing
    credentials.

    This patch also uses the absence of a `RefPtr<ServerT>` in the `OperationSender`
    as a signal that we've already shut down, which works as an "atomic" indicator,
    but could be confusing. I'm happy to change it for something else if preferred.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D286920

